# Definition contract

Return ONLY valid JSON with this shape:

```json
{
  "title": "string",
  "reportType": "all_workflows|specific_workflow|all_repositories|specific_repository",
  "sources": [
    {
      "alias": "string",
      "schemaName": "string|null",
      "table": "string"
    }
  ],
  "joins": [
    {
      "left": "alias.column",
      "right": "alias.column",
      "type": "inner|left"
    }
  ],
  "columns": [
    {
      "key": "string",
      "label": "string",
      "source": "alias.column",
      "aggregate": "none|count|sum|avg|min|max"
    }
  ],
  "filters": [
    {
      "field": "alias.column",
      "op": "eq|ne|gt|gte|lt|lte|in|like|is_null|not_null",
      "value": null
    }
  ],
  "groupBy": ["alias.column"],
  "orderBy": [
    {
      "field": "alias.column|columnKey",
      "direction": "asc|desc"
    }
  ],
  "availableFilters": [
    {
      "key": "string",
      "label": "string",
      "field": "alias.column",
      "type": "text|number|date|enum"
    }
  ],
  "summary": {},
  "warnings": ["string"]
}
```

- Top-level keys must match this contract.
- `columns` must be non-empty when the schema can support the request.
- `aggregate` defaults to `none` when omitted conceptually; always emit it explicitly.
- `joins`, `filters`, `groupBy`, `orderBy`, `availableFilters`, `summary`, and `warnings` may be empty arrays/objects but must be present.
- Do not wrap JSON in markdown fences.
- Do not emit SQL or extra keys.
